.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NQSEAL2 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqseal2 ,
.Nm nqseal3 ,
.Nm nqcapid
.Nd seal a format 2 or format 3 capsule, and a capsule's id
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Bd -literal
typedef struct {
  uint8_t id[32];
  const char *name;
} nqcin;
.Ed
.Pp
.Ft int
.Fo nqseal2
.Fa "const char *dir" "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const char *meta"
.Fa "const nqcin *in" "size_t nin"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqseal3
.Fa "const char *dir" "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const char *meta"
.Fa "const nqcin *in" "size_t nin"
.Fa "const uint8_t *skey" "size_t skeylen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn nqcapid "const char *dir" "uint8_t id[32]"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqseal2
is
.Xr nqseal 3
in format 2
.Pq Ql noqtis-capsule-2 , Ql noqtis-seal-2 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5 :
the manifest also carries a Merkle tree over its file entries, and the
seal signs the manifest's head, which holds the tree's root and size but
not the list of files.
.Xr nqprove 3
can then show single files without the others' names, sizes or
digests.
Its leaves are not salted: anyone who can guess a file a proof does not
show (its path and content) can compute that file's leaf and confirm the
guess against the hashes on the proof's audit paths.
.Pp
.Fn nqseal3
is
.Fn nqseal2
in format 3
.Pq Ql noqtis-capsule-3 , Ql noqtis-seal-3 :
each file entry also carries a salt of 32 bytes, and its leaf is
SHA-256(0x02 || salt || entry), so that a proof lets no one confirm a
guess of the files it does not show.
With
.Fa skey
.Dv NULL
.Pq and Fa skeylen No 0
each salt is 32 fresh bytes from
.Xr nqrand 3 ;
otherwise
.Fa skey
is a salt key of 32 bytes
.Pq Fa skeylen No 32
and each salt is SHA3-256("noqtis-salt-3" || 0x00 ||
.Fa skey
|| path), so that the same files give the same manifest
(for reproducible capsules).
Keep the salt key secret: whoever has it can compute every salt.
.Pp
.Fa in Ns Bq 0..nin
are the capsules this one was made from, at most 1024, recorded in the
manifest's
.Ql inputs :
each
.Fa id
is an input's id from
.Fn nqcapid ,
and each
.Fa name
1 to 255 bytes of UTF-8 with no control character.
.Fa in
may be
.Dv NULL
when
.Fa nin
is 0.
.Xr nqchkx 3
follows these records with its
.Fa lin
folders.
.Pp
.Fn nqcapid
stores in
.Fa id
the id of the capsule in
.Fa dir :
the SHA-256 of the bytes its seal signs
.Pq Ql manifest_sha256 No of a format 1 seal, Ql head_sha256 No of a format 2 or 3 one ,
read from
.Pa noqtis.sig .
Nothing else is checked: check the capsule
.Pq Xr nqchk 3
before relying on it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn nqseal2
and
.Fn nqseal3
return what
.Xr nqseal 3
returns, and
.Er NQEARG
for an input name that is empty, too long or has a control character
(and for
.Fn nqseal3 ,
a salt key not of 32 bytes), and
.Er NQELIM
for more than 1024 inputs.
.Fn nqcapid
returns
.Dv NQOK ,
.Er NQEIO
when the seal cannot be read,
.Er NQEDEC
when it is not a seal of either format, or
.Er NQEARG .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqchkx 3 ,
.Xr nqprove 3 ,
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
.Sh STANDARDS
The salted leaves of format 3 follow the salted digests of selective
disclosure (ISO/IEC 18013-5, SD-JWT); see
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5 .
.Rs
.%A B. Laurie
.%A E. Messeri
.%A R. Stradling
.%T Certificate Transparency Version 2.0
.%R RFC 9162
.%D December 2021
.Re
